&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Segoe UI',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Segoe UI',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Segoe UI',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;Income taxes are&amp;#8239;accrued&amp;#8239;in accordance with&amp;#8239;the FERC Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowance&amp;#8239;permitting&amp;#8239;the accrual of income taxes on a pass-through entity and the associated taxes&amp;#8239;accrued&amp;#8239;are treated as&amp;#8239;deemed&amp;#8239;contributions from the owners,&amp;#8239;whereas&amp;#8239;net operating loss carryovers are treated as&amp;#8239;deemed&amp;#8239;distributions. The deemed contribution recorded was $41.7&amp;#8239;million in 2025&amp;#8239;and $39.4&amp;#8239;million in 2024&amp;#8239;and was included within Other Paid-In Capital in the Comparative Balance Sheet. We will make all necessary adjustments to account balances upon a ruling in Docket No. AC18-228-000.&amp;#8239;&amp;#8239;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 16.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;&amp;#8239;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;On December 22, 2017, the United States enacted the &amp;#8220;Tax Cuts and Jobs Act&amp;#8221; (&amp;#8220;TCJA &amp;#8221;). The changes in the TCJA are effective for taxation years beginning after December 31, 2017. While the changes are broad and complex, the most&amp;#8239;significant change&amp;#8239;is the reduction in the corporate federal income tax rate from 35% to 21%. We recorded a $196.7 million decrease to our 2017 deferred income tax liability, a $55.3 million increase to our 2017 deferred income tax asset and an&amp;#8239;offsetting&amp;#8239;increase of $252.0 million to our regulatory liability.&amp;#8239;&amp;#8239;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 16.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;&amp;#8239;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;In 2018&amp;#8239;pursuant to&amp;#8239;guidance&amp;#8239;established&amp;#8239;in FERC Docket No. PL19-2-000, we began amortizing the regulated liability&amp;#8239;utilizing&amp;#8239;the reverse South Georgia flowback&amp;#8239;methodology&amp;#8239;over the&amp;#8239;46.6 year&amp;#8239;remaining life of the assets. In 2025&amp;#8239;and 2024, respectively, we recorded a $5.4 million decrease to regulatory liability, a $1.2 million decrease to our deferred income tax&amp;#8239;asset&amp;#8239;and an&amp;#8239;offsetting&amp;#8239;$4.2 million benefit to our deferred federal tax expense.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Segoe UI',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Segoe UI',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;7. Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; border: 1pt none windowtext; padding: 0in; background: #c6c6c6;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Segoe UI',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;Gulfstream Management &amp;amp; Operating Services, L.L.C. ("GMOS"), owned 50% by SEP and 50% by Williams&amp;#160;Partners&amp;#160;provides management, construction and operating services&amp;#160;pursuant to&amp;#160;agreements entered with us and with affiliates of Spectra Energy and Williams. GMOS bills us for services&amp;#160;rendered&amp;#160;including labor and benefit costs, employee expenses, overhead costs and in some cases, third-party costs. Such amounts are reflected in the Statement of Income for the year as Operation and Maintenance Expenses or in the Comparative Balance Sheet as Utility Plant, as&amp;#160;appropriate.&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Segoe UI',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
